12. SQLITE DEVELOPMENT RULES

SQLite is the development database.

This is intentional.

During development:

Fast iteration
Schema changes
Breaking changes
Testing
Local experimentation

are expected.

However:

SQLite ≠ PostgreSQL

Do not assume every PostgreSQL behavior exists identically in SQLite.

Avoid unnecessary database-specific SQL.

Foreign-key enforcement must be enabled during SQLite testing.

Production compatibility must eventually be tested against PostgreSQL.

---

13. MIGRATION RULES

Every schema change must go through Alembic.

Never manually modify a database schema and consider the work complete.

Never rewrite an already-applied migration to change history.

Correct approach:

Existing migration
        ↓
New requirement
        ↓
New Alembic migration

not:

Existing migration
        ↓
Edit old migration

