18. FINANCIAL DATA RULE

Financial records are special.

Never casually:

DELETE contribution
UPDATE historical amount
overwrite transaction

If a financial record is wrong, the correct future mechanism may involve:

reversal
adjustment
refund
correction
audit record

Do not invent the exact correction mechanism.

Follow the financial design in the applicable version.

---

19. PAYMENT RULE

Never assume:

User says payment succeeded
        =
Payment succeeded

Payment success must eventually be established using trusted provider information.

The planned architecture is:

Member
   ↓
Contribution
   ↓
Payment
   ↓
PaymentAttempt
   ↓
ProviderTransaction
   ↓
LedgerEntry

Provider-specific implementations must remain behind the provider abstraction.

---

20. IDEMPOTENCY RULE

External financial events can arrive more than once.

For example:

Payment callback
Payment callback
Payment callback

The system must not create three financial transactions.

Provider transactions should have an appropriate uniqueness rule such as:

(provider, provider_transaction_id)

being unique.

Never implement callback processing as:

create_transaction()

without checking whether that transaction has already been processed.

